<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοκρᾰτ-έομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		 with fut.
		
			Med.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κρατήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					8.48
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				34.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.99
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κρατηθήσομαι</span>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.75
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεδημοκράτημαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					52.13
				</span></i>
			:—<i>have a democratic constitution,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				642
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				12.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις
			δημοκρατουμένη</span> Lex ap.<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.88
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> impers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοκρατεῖται</span>”
				<i>democratic principles prevail,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1265b38
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
